HackerOne does not classify bug bounties by a narrow "variable vulnerability" category, but instead sets payouts according to the overall severity (Low to Critical) and the specific asset impacted. In security research, "variable vulnerabilities" encompass memory mismanagement, environmental manipulation, and data type state issues. [1] 
Because HackerOne operates as a crowdsourced platform hosting thousands of independent corporate programs, individual company policies dictate exact cash prizes. Below is a complete list of known variable-handling vulnerabilities mapped to their standard severity tier and their 2026 HackerOne market payout ranges. [2, 3, 4, 5, 6] 
