## Variable Vulnerability Payout Matrix
The following table synthesizes the typical severity levels and reward ranges for variable vulnerabilities across mid-to-high tier programs (e.g., PayPal or Slack). [7, 8] 

| Vulnerability Type | Primary Root Cause | HackerOne Severity Tier | Standard Payout Range | Extreme/Max Payout |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Buffer Overflow (Stack/Heap) | Writing excess data past variable memory allocation. | Critical to High | $10,000 – $30,000+ | Up to $250,000+ (e.g., Google Chrome/Enterprise kernels) |
| Use-After-Free (UAF) | Program fails to clear a variable pointer after freeing memory. | Critical to High | $8,000 – $25,000 | Up to $150,000+ (Browsers / OS Kernels) |
| Integer Overflow / Underflow | Numeric variable exceeds maximum storage bits and flips value. | High to Medium | $1,000 – $15,000 | Millions (if targeting Crypto/Smart Contracts via Immunefi[](https://sqmagazine.co.uk/smart-contract-bug-bounties-statistics/)) |
| Race Condition (TOCTOU) | Variable changes state between a check and its usage. | High to Medium | $2,000 – $12,000 | Up to $30,000+ (Fintech/Payment bypasses) |
| Environment Variable Injection | Modifying systemic variables to load malicious libraries. | Medium to Low | $500 – $5,000 | Program-dependent |
| Uninitialized Variable Use | Reading memory from a variable container before assigning a value. | Medium to Low | $250 – $3,000 | Context-dependent (Information Disclosure) |
| Type Confusion | Variable allocated as one object type but accessed as another. | Critical to High | $5,000 – $20,000 | Up to $100,000+ (V8 Engine / WebKit) |

